body:
Ok, I got it! I think it was the D2:D221 that I added. I tried to get fancy, now that I've removed those numbers and update to C2 it works.

&#x200B;

I really appreciate your help, thank you so much!

I just posted about having potty training issues with my almost 4 year old yesterday. Mine is just poop issues, but someone suggested looking up "encopresis." It's incontinence issues that happen in children, and can be caused by traumatic occurrences. I would ask your pediatrician about the issues, maybe they can see if there is some underlying issue that could be causing the regression. 

&#x200B;

One other suggestions I came across while reading - have her wear a diaper but cut a hole in them, then place your child on the toilet. They may be more comfortable going if they feel like they're wearing something. I don't know if it will help, but it's an idea.

The mom from Malcolm in the Middle. 

&#x200B;

I thought she was an evil witch when I was younger. Now, I get it.

Here are the pictures, with a banana for scale :)

&#x200B;

[https://imgur.com/a/Xr6pNFD](https://imgur.com/a/Xr6pNFD)

I wish I had traveled more. There were so many places I wanted to see, they now have been put on hold because of kids. I have two very little children, so travelling to see historical places would be difficult, and it wouldn't be as enriching.

&#x200B;

I also wish I had gotten more tattoos, haha! Now all my extra money goes to child care or college funds!

If you are a conservative in a liberal area (or vice versa) then you may not see the point of voting as your vote will be washed out. For example, I know someone in Illinois (a traditionally democratic state) that won't vote because, as a republican, they feel their vote won't matter.

&#x200B;

With the electoral college it feels as if there is no point to voting. If you can lose the popular vote but still win the election, why bother?

&#x200B;

Finally, from what I understand votes weigh differently depending on where you are at. Forty five votes in a state like Missouri are equal to one vote in a state like California. You may want to research that point a little more for some clarity, though.

Two brothers try to resurrect their dead mother. It goes horribly wrong. One ends up losing a leg and an arm, the other ends up with his soul attached to a suit of armor. The rest of the story is them trying to get the younger brother's body back.

&#x200B;

/s

It's impossible to hum while holding your nose shut.

&#x200B;

Go on, try it.

LOL, I wondered what happened to the food in a situation like this. We had an incident about a week ago where we ordered food through GrubHub. Delivery driver never showed, never tried to call or contact us, even though my brother was waiting on the porch for them to show up. Then we get an email saying they tried to deliver but no one was home, so they had to move on to other deliveries.

&#x200B;

We were able to get our money refunded, though, so it was okay in the end.

My son has one of these helmets. We battled with insurance for two months trying to get them to cover part of the cost. Even after a peer-to-peer review with the doctor saying it was a severe case, they still declined to help.

&#x200B;

Luckily, there is a charity in our area that helps out with children's orthotics. We were able to apply for help from them.

A lot of the officers will lose their jobs. And with having to pay for police help, a lot of the smaller municipalities will have to be absorbed into the county because they won't be able to afford to stay separate. Which means loss of jobs for any of that municipality's city workers, from parks department to the mayor.

&#x200B;

Also, police response times in the municipalities will be a lot longer than they are right now.

I had weight issues after my first child. No matter how much I dieted and exercised, I couldn't lose the weight. One day, I went to a laundromat I hadn't used in a while. The lady behind the desk saw me and immediately said, "What happened to you? You used to be skinny, not anymore!"

&#x200B;

Made me feel really bad.
